Audio signals are often affected by background noise such as traffic, crowd, and environmental disturbances, which degrade speech quality. This project proposes a deep learning-based noise cancellation system using an Autoencoder. The model is trained on clean and noisy speech data to learn meaningful representations of speech signals. Audio signals are converted into spectrograms, and the autoencoder reconstructs clean speech from noisy input. The proposed system improves Signal-to-Noise Ratio (SNR) and enhances speech clarity, making it suitable for real-world communication and speech processing applications.
